---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';

const pageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Juan Esquivel',
  url: 'https://juanesquivel.xyz/about',
  description:
    'Background, taste, and working context for Juan Esquivel.',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Juan Esquivel',
    url: 'https://juanesquivel.xyz',
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About Juan Esquivel — Crypto Marketer in Los Angeles"
  description="Background, taste, and working context for Juan Esquivel."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(pageSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <Nav active="about" />

  <PageHeader title="About" subtitle="Background, taste, and the path into the work." />

  <article class="prose">
    <p class="lead">
      I'm Juan. From Los Angeles, child of Mexican immigrants, raised by the internet, and now back
      in LA.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've been doing marketing in crypto for about four years now. Got in through content. Writing
      was the way in and it's still the thing I keep circling back to. These days I'm more drawn to
      brand and product marketing, but storytelling runs through all of it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Studied finance in school. Graduated around DeFi summer which was good timing I guess. The
      traditional finance path never really appealed to me. My parents got burned by 2008 and the
      opportunities I was seeing just felt off. Meanwhile crypto Twitter was going crazy. I knew I
      wanted in somehow.
    </p>

    <p>
      I spent time away and got a lot out of the reset, but I'm back in Los Angeles now. Being home
      again feels clarifying. The city still shapes my taste, my references, and probably the way I
      think about brand more than anywhere else.
    </p>

    <p>
      When I'm not working I'm usually watching movies, digging through music, or hunting for good
      coffee shops around the city. In another life I helped run an indie electronic label with some
      friends in London. Tried my hand at DJing. I watch too much baseball, too many streamers, and
      I've seen every episode of Seinfeld more times than I'd admit. Have traveled to over 13
      countries and counting.
    </p>

    <p>
      The throughline is still the same: storytelling, creativity, world-building, brand. The part
      of work that doesn't feel like work.
    </p>

    <p class="resume-link"><a href="/resume" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View my resume →</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .resume-link {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .resume-link a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .resume-link a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
